          "filename": "A summer evening in St Mary's Place - geograph.org.uk - 5520825.jpg",
          "caption": "View across Lace Market Square in the English city of Nottingham. Photographed from the squares south side (also known as St Mary's Place) it shows the east side, crossed by St Mary's Gate. Along this side is T C Hine's Adams Building, a lace factory of 1857. The attic (or lantern or clerestory) finishing rooms with their continuous strips of windows had daylight longest and there the finest work was done. These are west-facing and catch the last of light at ten past eight on a fine late-summer evening.",
          "alt": "View across Lace Market Square in the English city of Nottingham. Photographed from the squares south side (also known as St Mary's Place) it shows the east side, crossed by St Mary's Gate. Along this side is T C Hine's Adams Building, a lace factory of 1857. The attic (or lantern or clerestory) finishing rooms with their continuous strips of windows had daylight longest and there the finest work was done. These are west-facing and catch the last of light at ten past eight on a fine late-summer evening.",
